# Models and sliced output live in OneDrive\3D printing\, not here.
# This repo is documentation and slicer configuration only.
*.stl
*.3mf
*.gcode
*.step
*.obj
*.zip

# PrusaSlicer physical-printer configs hold plaintext API keys — never commit.
physical_printer/
*physical_printer*
# ...and the stand-in for one that scripts/mk3s-resume/printer.ini.example says how to make.
scripts/mk3s-resume/printer.ini

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# scad-preview.sh scratch output
preview/

# OpenSCAD Customizer parameter sets. The GUI writes these automatically, which
# makes them a SECOND source of truth that only the GUI reads — the CLI ignores
# them unless given -p/-P. One went stale here holding a superseded design plus
# a parameter that had since been renamed, so the preset silently set a variable
# nothing read. The .scad is the source of truth.
*.json

# Vendor datasheets and any other third-party document. This is COPYRIGHT, not
# privacy, which is why it is handled differently from a secret: dropping the
# file from HEAD achieves nothing, because the problem is distributing someone
# else's document at all. A history rewrite already purged this exact set once.
# Extract the DATA into Markdown instead and link where the original came from —
# facts are free to use. That is also a size argument: 2.6 MB of Inslogic PDF
# became 7.8 KB of slicer/reference/inslogic-filament-data.md, which is greppable
# and diffable where the PDFs are neither.
# Deliberately repo-wide and by extension rather than naming the four files: the
# four are not special, and a rule that lists them protects against those four
# and nothing else. Nothing in this repo should ever track a PDF (verified: zero
# tracked, zero anywhere in history). Both cases are spelled out rather than
# relying on core.ignorecase, which is a per-host setting.
*.pdf
*.PDF

